WEBVTT

00:07.298 --> 00:09.926
[distant sirens wailing]

00:10.010 --> 00:12.137
[officer 1] You fucker, hold still!
Stay still, punk!

00:12.220 --> 00:13.888
[officer 2] You're under arrest
for murder.

00:14.389 --> 00:15.974
You have the right to an attorney.

00:16.057 --> 00:17.308
[man 1] Let go of me!

00:17.392 --> 00:18.727
[whistle blowing]

00:18.810 --> 00:20.812
[man 1 yelling indistinctly]

00:21.771 --> 00:23.940
- Let go of me!
- [officer 2] We need backup.

00:24.024 --> 00:26.443
[whooshing]

00:26.526 --> 00:27.569
[man 1] Fuck you!

00:27.652 --> 00:28.903
[officer 3] Grab the kid.

00:28.987 --> 00:30.071
[man 2 panting]

00:30.155 --> 00:32.323
[somber music playing]

00:32.407 --> 00:34.826
- My mom and dad…
- [man 1 yelling indistinctly]

00:35.577 --> 00:36.661
My brother…

00:36.745 --> 00:38.246
You have to save them.

00:38.329 --> 00:39.164
[man 1 screams]

00:39.247 --> 00:41.750
- [typewriter keys clacking]
- [phone ringing]

00:42.959 --> 00:43.960
[officer 4] Thanks.

00:44.753 --> 00:46.046
Get a fucking move on.

00:46.629 --> 00:49.674
[officer 5] If you'd like to be a witness,
we could arrange that too.

00:51.468 --> 00:54.721
Hey, everybody ready?
Cho, how's the statement going?

00:54.804 --> 00:57.057
Yeah, we're almost there.

00:57.140 --> 00:59.934
[officer 6] Why are you still wearing
your bloody clothes?

01:00.018 --> 01:03.021
Reporters are everywhere.
We all have to be ready, understood?

01:03.104 --> 01:04.147
[officers] Yes, sir.

01:04.230 --> 01:06.232
[indistinct chatter]

01:08.860 --> 01:09.861
Listen,

01:10.653 --> 01:13.448
I'll… take you to the hospital
as soon as I'm done.

01:13.948 --> 01:15.909
All you have to do is sit tight, hmm?

01:16.493 --> 01:17.452
Okay.

01:17.535 --> 01:18.703
[officer 7] Okay, great.

01:19.204 --> 01:20.747
And what time did this happen?

01:21.831 --> 01:23.583
[uneasy music playing]

01:27.504 --> 01:29.506
[tense music playing]

01:37.931 --> 01:39.390
[prisoner] Detective Cho!

01:39.474 --> 01:41.059
The kid has a gun!

01:43.311 --> 01:44.604
No! Don't!

01:44.687 --> 01:45.730
Don't do it!

01:45.814 --> 01:46.773
Nobody move!

01:47.273 --> 01:48.316
[breathing shakily]

01:48.399 --> 01:49.317
Do…

01:49.400 --> 01:50.985
- [prisoner] Hey.
- [Cho] Lee Do!

01:51.069 --> 01:52.821
Look at me, okay? Huh?

01:52.904 --> 01:53.738
Come on.

01:53.822 --> 01:55.198
[Cho] Shut your fucking mouth!

01:56.157 --> 01:57.659
[prisoner laughs] Shoot me.

01:57.742 --> 01:59.369
- What are you waiting for?
- [Cho] Lee Do!

01:59.452 --> 02:00.328
[music fades]

02:00.411 --> 02:01.538
Go ahead.

02:02.122 --> 02:04.457
[sobs, screams]

02:06.626 --> 02:07.877
[gunshot]

02:09.546 --> 02:10.672
[tense music playing]

02:10.755 --> 02:12.757
[officer] Shooting at Yeongseong Gosiwon.

02:12.841 --> 02:15.176
All units in the area,
report to the scene immediately.

02:15.260 --> 02:17.804
I repeat, shooting at Yeongseong Gosiwon.

02:17.887 --> 02:18.763
All units in the area…

02:18.847 --> 02:20.849
[people screaming]

02:22.725 --> 02:23.685
[automatic gunfire]

02:24.352 --> 02:25.979
[man 1 screams]

02:27.605 --> 02:28.648
[man 2 grunting]

02:33.361 --> 02:35.071
What's going on? Are you okay?!

02:35.155 --> 02:36.239
[gunfire]

02:40.785 --> 02:42.078
[chuckling]

02:47.041 --> 02:48.877
[officer 1] Officer Kim! Officer Kim!

02:48.960 --> 02:51.004
[man 3] Get out of here, man! Oh God!

02:52.088 --> 02:53.464
- Where is the shooter?
- He's inside.

02:53.548 --> 02:54.799
[officer 1] Okay, let's go!

03:01.598 --> 03:02.515
Spread out!

03:07.937 --> 03:09.314
[music fades]

03:09.981 --> 03:10.857
My life…

03:10.940 --> 03:12.942
[thunder rumbling]

03:13.026 --> 03:14.235
[somber music playing]

03:14.319 --> 03:16.404
…is finally ending on a high note.

03:17.488 --> 03:18.364
[officer 2] You there.

03:19.282 --> 03:20.450
Drop your weapon!

03:25.038 --> 03:25.955
Finally…

03:27.081 --> 03:28.249
[officer 2] Don't move!

03:29.250 --> 03:30.835
You know, these guns are

03:32.420 --> 03:34.464
surprisingly easy to use.

03:35.882 --> 03:36.883
So easy.

03:36.966 --> 03:39.052
[officer 2] Drop the gun
and put your hands up!

03:39.135 --> 03:41.137
I heard the first rounds you guys shoot…

03:41.971 --> 03:42.847
[music stops]

03:42.931 --> 03:44.807
…are always the ones filled with blanks.

03:44.891 --> 03:46.309
- What?
- [gun clicks]

03:46.392 --> 03:48.394
[dramatic music playing]

03:49.979 --> 03:51.022
[officer 3 grunts]

03:52.106 --> 03:53.983
[siren wailing]

04:00.990 --> 04:01.991
Get down!

04:02.533 --> 04:03.576
Get out! Get out!

04:06.913 --> 04:07.997
Why save any of you?

04:08.081 --> 04:09.499
You're nothing but trash.

04:10.500 --> 04:13.086
[officer] All units! An officer was shot!

04:13.169 --> 04:16.172
The suspect is
currently armed with a machine gun.

04:17.632 --> 04:19.092
- [officer grunting]
- [Do] You okay?

04:19.175 --> 04:20.635
- Yes.
- And the people inside?

04:20.718 --> 04:22.720
They're all too scared
to come out right now.

04:23.596 --> 04:25.056
[automatic gunfire]

04:25.139 --> 04:26.975
[Jeong-tae] Come out, you fuckers!

04:28.142 --> 04:29.143
Just wait here.

04:29.227 --> 04:31.854
- What? Officer Lee!
- [Jeong-tae] Think I won't find you?

04:31.938 --> 04:33.564
- Huh?
- [automatic gunfire]

04:34.232 --> 04:36.234
[woman screams, whimpers]

04:39.862 --> 04:41.072
[Jeong-tae] I told you.

04:41.155 --> 04:43.408
You shouldn't have ignored
everything I said.

04:44.867 --> 04:47.412
This would have never happened
if you'd all been more considerate.

04:47.495 --> 04:49.038
- [automatic gunfire]
- [glass shattering]

04:50.206 --> 04:52.208
All of you people drove me to this!

04:52.875 --> 04:54.919
Did I ask for something unreasonable?!

04:55.003 --> 04:57.171
- [automatic gunfire]
- [woman whimpering]

04:57.255 --> 04:58.381
[woman screams]

04:59.841 --> 05:02.760
All you needed to do
was not touch other people's food.

05:03.428 --> 05:05.972
- Not talk loudly in shared spaces!
- [automatic gunfire]

05:06.472 --> 05:09.350
Not talk loudly in shared spaces.
Is that so hard?

05:12.312 --> 05:13.938
There's no hope here.

05:14.022 --> 05:14.981
[exhales]

05:15.064 --> 05:17.233
[Jeong-tae] It doesn't exist
in this place.

05:20.028 --> 05:22.947
Your lives are drowning, just like mine.

05:24.699 --> 05:26.117
I'll set you all free

05:27.160 --> 05:29.078
by killing each and every one of you.

05:29.871 --> 05:31.414
[tense music playing]

05:35.960 --> 05:38.629
I'll find you all,
no matter how well you hide.

05:40.214 --> 05:42.216
[breathing shakily]

05:49.057 --> 05:50.641
[man 4 exclaims in alarm]

05:52.852 --> 05:54.103
[man 4] Please spare me!

05:54.187 --> 05:55.480
[automatic gunfire]

05:57.023 --> 05:58.524
Listen to me carefully.

05:59.192 --> 06:00.443
The shooter has an M4.

06:00.526 --> 06:02.737
He's fired three rounds
and is left with 27.

06:02.820 --> 06:04.155
- [man screams]
- [automatic gunfire]

06:04.238 --> 06:05.323
[officers exclaim in panic]

06:06.491 --> 06:07.658
Twenty-four now.

06:08.284 --> 06:11.329
I'll make him waste his ammo
while you guys rescue the others.

06:11.412 --> 06:13.206
Officer Lee, maybe there's another way?

06:13.289 --> 06:16.459
Don't worry about me. We have to save
as many of them as possible.

06:16.959 --> 06:18.419
[music fades]

06:21.756 --> 06:23.633
[uneasy music playing]

06:23.716 --> 06:24.717
What is this?

06:26.803 --> 06:28.096
[lights plinking]

06:51.828 --> 06:54.080
[tense music playing]

07:05.007 --> 07:06.717
[panting]

07:06.801 --> 07:08.845
[yelling furiously]

07:10.054 --> 07:11.139
[gun clicks]

07:15.059 --> 07:16.018
[magazine clatters]

07:16.102 --> 07:17.812
[dramatic music playing]

07:27.613 --> 07:28.906
[panting]

07:33.327 --> 07:34.328
Damn you!

07:37.373 --> 07:38.374
Hey!

07:46.340 --> 07:48.384
Come on. Come on!

07:48.468 --> 07:49.469
[Jeong-u] This way.

07:58.019 --> 07:59.312
[music fades]

08:00.813 --> 08:02.148
[rapid footsteps]

08:03.733 --> 08:06.527
[Jeong-tae] Motherfucker!
You're not allowed to save anyone!

08:06.611 --> 08:07.695
[dramatic music resumes]

08:11.115 --> 08:12.325
[groans]

08:15.578 --> 08:16.996
Get in there! Hurry!

08:20.917 --> 08:22.001
[music subsides]

08:22.084 --> 08:23.085
I told you…

08:26.255 --> 08:28.299
[inspirational music playing]

08:31.052 --> 08:32.011
[yells] Oh!

08:36.182 --> 08:39.894
[sirens wailing]

08:39.977 --> 08:41.979
[indistinct chatter]

08:44.565 --> 08:45.566
Thank you.

08:46.275 --> 08:47.652
- Good work, officers.
- It's my duty.

08:47.735 --> 08:49.153
[officer 2] We need traffic control.

08:49.237 --> 08:51.697
- [officer 1] No photos!
- [officer 2] Make your way there ASAP.

08:54.408 --> 08:55.910
[man 1] Chief Yoon! Over here!

08:55.993 --> 08:58.329
- [woman 1] Chief Yoon!
- [woman 2] Chief Yoon!

08:58.412 --> 09:00.498
- [reporters shouting questions]
- [siren wailing]

09:02.041 --> 09:03.501
[exhales deeply]

09:05.878 --> 09:07.171
Security cameras?

09:07.255 --> 09:10.967
Well, they'll be difficult to obtain
since the computer was destroyed, sir.

09:11.050 --> 09:12.468
Any witnesses?

09:12.552 --> 09:15.263
No one is ready to make a statement,
so it'll take some time.

09:15.346 --> 09:17.056
[sighs] What a disaster.

09:18.975 --> 09:21.644
- [officer 1] Can we check the markings?
- [officer 2] On it, sir.

09:21.727 --> 09:23.354
[cameras clicking]

09:28.484 --> 09:30.820
[officer 3] We need to secure Unit 308
as well!

09:30.903 --> 09:32.905
[intriguing music playing]

09:48.713 --> 09:49.839
[officer 4] Finish up here.

09:49.922 --> 09:52.216
- And itemize everything.
- [officer 5] Yes, sir.

09:52.717 --> 09:54.302
[bed creaks]

09:55.553 --> 09:56.721
[hollow thuds]

10:05.688 --> 10:06.647
[sighs]

10:07.148 --> 10:08.232
I remember this.

10:08.316 --> 10:11.736
Stayed in a place just like it
when I was studying to get into the force.

10:12.320 --> 10:13.529
Trapped here all by yourself.

10:13.613 --> 10:16.574
[sighs] At times,
I felt like I was losing my mind.

10:19.285 --> 10:21.287
[suspenseful music playing]

10:22.246 --> 10:25.333
Back in your day,
did you sleep on plywood?

10:25.416 --> 10:28.419
No. I mean, who would do that?
It's not a coffin.

10:32.256 --> 10:33.132
[Jeong-u gasps]

10:34.383 --> 10:35.259
[Jeong-u] My God.

10:38.763 --> 10:39.847
Officer Jeong.

10:40.848 --> 10:42.767
Have you ever seen anything like this?

10:43.559 --> 10:45.770
- [music fades]
- Chief Yoon! More guns have been found.

10:45.853 --> 10:46.812
What?!

10:48.564 --> 10:52.026
[Seo] They've all been itemized.
You can check them yourself, sir.

10:52.818 --> 10:54.236
They're all automatic…

10:55.571 --> 10:58.157
Call the military
and ask them to send a gun expert.

10:58.240 --> 10:59.325
Yes, Chief.

11:00.493 --> 11:02.536
Hey, we need someone here who knows…

11:06.082 --> 11:07.833
- Listen.
- [inhales deeply]

11:11.420 --> 11:12.421
[Yoon] Who's this?

11:12.505 --> 11:14.256
I told you to get an expert in here.

11:14.340 --> 11:19.303
Uh… Officer Lee, uh, was in the military
before he became a police officer, sir.

11:19.387 --> 11:22.932
[Yoon] Then he can explain what he knows
before a real expert gets here.

11:23.432 --> 11:24.642
[Do sighs]

11:26.018 --> 11:28.229
What the hell is he doing?

11:28.312 --> 11:30.940
If you don't know what you're doing,
just stay out of it.

11:31.023 --> 11:32.316
All right, sir.

11:33.818 --> 11:35.111
Allow me to explain.

11:38.948 --> 11:40.658
[intriguing music playing]

11:58.884 --> 11:59.802
[whooshing]

12:10.146 --> 12:12.481
[intriguing music continues]

12:20.072 --> 12:22.074
[intriguing music continues]

12:32.418 --> 12:33.878
[music fades]

12:37.131 --> 12:38.591
Let me give you a rundown.

12:40.134 --> 12:43.012
This is the XM177,
used by the US special ops

12:43.095 --> 12:44.513
during the Vietnam War.

12:44.597 --> 12:47.057
And this is the AK-47,

12:47.141 --> 12:50.519
a 7.62-millimeter Kalashnikov,
produced by the Soviet Union.

12:50.603 --> 12:53.689
And this is, uh, the German MP5,

12:53.773 --> 12:55.691
first introduced back in 1964,

12:55.775 --> 12:58.694
iconically used for counterterrorism
across the world.

12:58.778 --> 13:01.864
And finally, the MK MOD 1,

13:01.947 --> 13:04.700
a special warfare standard-issue rifle.

13:04.784 --> 13:06.911
It's modified and modernized,

13:06.994 --> 13:09.121
widely used by US Special Forces.

13:09.205 --> 13:11.040
So you're saying that all of these guns,

13:11.123 --> 13:14.168
that were used in past conflicts
and wars around the world,

13:14.668 --> 13:16.754
were discovered here in Korea?

13:17.254 --> 13:19.548
That true? You believe that?

13:20.841 --> 13:21.717
Yes.

13:22.593 --> 13:23.803
There's something else.

13:23.886 --> 13:27.306
You remember the bullets
found at that suicide scene?

13:27.389 --> 13:30.434
The ones that we found
in the ceiling of that house?

13:30.518 --> 13:33.479
- [Do] Yes.
- We're still looking into that. Why?

13:36.982 --> 13:38.400
The bullets found on the scene

13:39.652 --> 13:41.195
fit the guns we have here.

13:43.155 --> 13:44.490
They're all compatible.

13:44.990 --> 13:47.117
[unsettling music playing]

13:51.455 --> 13:52.706
In my opinion,

13:53.958 --> 13:56.377
the two cases are strongly related.

13:57.878 --> 13:58.921
Okay.

13:59.880 --> 14:01.799
We're onto something important.

14:02.883 --> 14:04.677
No one can breathe a word of this.

14:04.760 --> 14:05.678
No journalists.

14:05.761 --> 14:06.887
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

14:07.429 --> 14:08.764
[Yoon] Let's wrap this up.

14:13.894 --> 14:14.937
[sighs]

14:20.025 --> 14:21.026
[man 1] Man, I'm starving.

14:21.110 --> 14:22.945
Fuck's sakes, when's he coming out?

14:23.612 --> 14:24.697
[man 1] Can I have some?

14:24.780 --> 14:27.700
- [man] Shocking news in Gyeongin gosiwon.
- Holy shit, take a look at this.

14:27.783 --> 14:29.243
Police have arrested the shooter.

14:29.326 --> 14:32.037
A student resident of the gosiwon
was caught on the scene…

14:32.121 --> 14:33.080
MASS SHOOTING AT GOSIWON

14:33.163 --> 14:36.542
- He is presently in police custody.
- Hmm. Are we living in the US or what?

14:36.625 --> 14:39.545
Fuck, I have a bad feeling
about this shit.

14:39.628 --> 14:41.297
- I really do.
- [man 2] Don't be so dramatic.

14:42.047 --> 14:42.882
[man 3] Oh shit.

14:42.965 --> 14:46.010
- [man 4] Shooting people in the back?
- [man 3] Look at this. It's fucking crazy.

14:51.432 --> 14:54.351
- Hey, go see what's going on.
- Yes, sir.

14:59.690 --> 15:00.941
- [clattering]
- [glass shatters]

15:01.025 --> 15:02.693
[man 5] Stand up, you bastard!

15:03.402 --> 15:06.322
Let go, you fucking goons!
You'll pay for this!

15:06.405 --> 15:07.781
Shut the fuck up!

15:07.865 --> 15:09.283
I know who you all are!

15:09.867 --> 15:11.660
Yong-gu, you fucking bastard!

15:12.161 --> 15:13.245
For God's sake!

15:13.746 --> 15:15.539
Stop this! Hey!

15:16.040 --> 15:17.750
Please stop this madness!

15:17.833 --> 15:20.419
[whimpering]
I know you still have some humanity!

15:20.502 --> 15:22.755
Please! Let's talk. Huh?

15:23.422 --> 15:26.091
Let's go inside, a… and we can
both have a drink, and we can--

15:26.175 --> 15:29.261
Oh, drinking is the worst.
You should really give that up.

15:29.345 --> 15:30.179
What do you want?

15:30.262 --> 15:33.682
Things would be different if you'd
handed over the business I asked for.

15:33.766 --> 15:34.975
We can still negotiate!

15:35.476 --> 15:36.393
[groans]

15:37.645 --> 15:39.104
You fucking bastards!

15:39.188 --> 15:41.607
Let go of me! God dammit!

15:42.107 --> 15:43.192
Damn you!

15:43.275 --> 15:45.611
[whimpering]

15:47.821 --> 15:50.908
Oh! Good work, everyone.

15:50.991 --> 15:52.618
- Go home now.
- [man 5] Yes, sir.

15:53.577 --> 15:55.037
- Yong-gu.
- Sir.

15:55.120 --> 15:57.706
Once I sort this out,
the business is yours.

15:57.790 --> 15:58.916
Yes, sir.

16:00.542 --> 16:02.711
Let's go.
And don't forget to take care of this guy.

16:02.795 --> 16:05.339
- [men] Yes, sir.
- I curse you, you son of a bitch!

16:05.422 --> 16:07.341
- You're a fucking traitor!
- [chuckling]

16:07.424 --> 16:08.884
Motherfucker!

16:09.551 --> 16:12.388
- Get this off of me, you bastards!
- [chuckling]

16:12.471 --> 16:14.056
- [engine starts]
- [captive groaning]

16:14.139 --> 16:15.683
Get this off of me!

16:16.266 --> 16:18.811
- [captive groaning]
- [men grunting]

16:19.603 --> 16:21.063
Okay, it's time to get ready.

16:21.146 --> 16:23.190
- [captive groaning]
- Come on!

16:29.321 --> 16:30.447
[man 3] Game on.

16:30.531 --> 16:31.532
[man 4] Let's go.

16:33.659 --> 16:35.411
Here we go, yo!

16:35.494 --> 16:36.787
- Fuck yeah!
- [man 3] All right.

16:36.870 --> 16:38.747
- [man grunts]
- On three. One two…

16:38.831 --> 16:39.832
[men grunt]

16:40.541 --> 16:43.002
- Ah, this job is a pain in the ass.
- Hey, gofers.

16:44.503 --> 16:48.215
Don't forget your mops and brooms.
It's pretty messy in there today.

16:48.716 --> 16:50.092
[Yong-gu chuckling]

16:50.175 --> 16:51.927
Oh, shut your mouth, you asshole.

16:52.011 --> 16:55.014
You take your sweet-ass time,
and then tell us to hurry up?

16:55.097 --> 16:56.056
Don't stress about it.

16:56.140 --> 16:58.183
[tuts] Fucking losers.

16:58.267 --> 17:00.811
- Yeah.
- Don't you look at me with your ugly face!

17:08.402 --> 17:10.112
[slurps]

17:10.195 --> 17:13.240
[Seo] Are you out of your damn mind?
Who ordered this for him?

17:14.324 --> 17:16.285
This isn't a restaurant, huh?

17:16.368 --> 17:18.454
[officer 1] He said he'd cooperate
if we ordered food.

17:18.537 --> 17:20.873
- Get that out. Captain Joo is on his way.
- Sorry, sir.

17:22.332 --> 17:23.417
[Joo sighs]

17:24.460 --> 17:25.294
You.

17:26.754 --> 17:27.755
What's your deal?

17:28.881 --> 17:30.632
Where'd you get that gun?

17:31.467 --> 17:32.468
The gun?

17:34.720 --> 17:35.971
[sighs]

17:40.726 --> 17:41.727
I told you.

17:43.687 --> 17:45.314
I'll only talk to that guy.

17:50.527 --> 17:51.945
We meet again.

17:53.072 --> 17:54.740
Why did you ask to see me?

17:55.365 --> 17:58.160
I wasn't really aware of it
in the heat of the moment,

17:59.495 --> 18:02.581
but when you grabbed my face
and put it into the wall… Bang!

18:02.664 --> 18:04.374
…all I could think of was…

18:06.376 --> 18:08.295
this guy's the real deal.

18:09.838 --> 18:12.674
He works on a whole other level.
Someone I can respect.

18:13.759 --> 18:15.177
[laughs manically]

18:18.222 --> 18:19.139
[Joo scoffs]

18:19.223 --> 18:21.350
Do you hear the same shit I'm hearing?

18:23.227 --> 18:25.813
I'm happy to talk
as long as it's you asking the questions.

18:30.150 --> 18:31.110
[Joo] Turn it up.

18:32.027 --> 18:33.362
[volume control turns]

18:36.448 --> 18:37.533
Where did you get the gun?

18:37.616 --> 18:39.243
It was couriered to me.

18:40.536 --> 18:41.787
And who sent it?

18:43.580 --> 18:44.581
Don't know.

18:44.665 --> 18:47.042
I don't know how much longer
I can listen to this shit.

18:47.835 --> 18:53.423
Why would a stranger send you a package
with a gun in it by courier? The truth.

18:54.299 --> 18:56.343
Why it showed up, I don't really know.

18:59.429 --> 19:01.181
It's probably
because I desperately wanted it.

19:01.765 --> 19:03.684
Shouldn't this guy be medicated?

19:04.393 --> 19:07.229
[sighs] I don't know.
None of this seems real.

19:08.689 --> 19:09.690
Jeong-tae.

19:12.568 --> 19:14.862
- This isn't a time for joking around.
- [tense music playing]

19:14.945 --> 19:16.655
If you knew anything about me,

19:17.739 --> 19:20.117
you'd know I take things very seriously.

19:28.041 --> 19:29.751
What's your history with guns?

19:31.587 --> 19:34.131
Far, near, middle.
Far, near, middle. [laughs]

19:34.631 --> 19:35.841
Like the military.

19:36.717 --> 19:38.719
[tense music continues]

19:41.013 --> 19:44.016
Were the guns hidden under your bed
also couriered to you?

19:44.725 --> 19:45.851
[sighs deeply]

19:46.560 --> 19:48.520
You see, that's the weird part.

19:49.563 --> 19:51.231
I definitely said… I definitely said

19:51.315 --> 19:53.400
that I would just like
one decent one for protection,

19:54.067 --> 19:56.445
so I don't really know why
they sent me so many.

19:59.698 --> 20:01.950
Just thinking about it makes me angry.

20:05.579 --> 20:07.581
[sighs] Jeong-tae.

20:09.291 --> 20:11.627
Do you know how many people died
because of you?

20:13.128 --> 20:15.631
If you feel sorry at all
about what you've done to them,

20:16.256 --> 20:18.884
you should answer my questions truthfully.

20:20.135 --> 20:20.969
Fuck them all.

20:21.053 --> 20:22.554
[music intensifies]

20:24.306 --> 20:27.309
Do you think those bastards felt sorry
about what they did?

20:28.560 --> 20:31.897
Those assholes who had no respect
for the law, rules, or even common sense!

20:32.773 --> 20:33.774
Fuck them.

20:35.067 --> 20:36.151
Whatever your reason,

20:36.235 --> 20:38.737
you can't justify shooting so many people.

20:38.820 --> 20:41.615
Have you been listening
to what I said at all?!

20:43.158 --> 20:45.953
Just like you guys catch criminals
and put them away,

20:46.036 --> 20:47.913
I did the same thing
to a bunch of scumbags.

20:47.996 --> 20:50.374
Do you know how many people I saved?

20:50.457 --> 20:52.668
By killing off just 20 of those scumbags,

20:52.751 --> 20:54.628
I've made hundreds of people safe.

20:54.711 --> 20:56.964
So why… why don't you ask me about that?!

20:57.756 --> 21:00.509
[breathing deeply]

21:02.344 --> 21:04.846
What I did is no different
than what you do.

21:05.514 --> 21:07.516
I did exactly what the police failed to.

21:11.144 --> 21:12.646
You think we're alike?

21:14.273 --> 21:15.649
You don't think we are?

21:18.777 --> 21:21.238
Will you at least admit that I'm a…

21:22.614 --> 21:24.324
a champion of justice?

21:24.408 --> 21:26.410
[tense music continues]

21:27.786 --> 21:28.870
[Jeong-tae sighs]

21:29.663 --> 21:32.082
There are… more guns out there.

21:33.667 --> 21:34.793
[Do] What do you mean?

21:37.504 --> 21:39.256
There are more people out there with guns.

21:39.840 --> 21:41.091
Do you know this for sure?

21:46.847 --> 21:47.764
[Yoon] What's he doing?

21:50.642 --> 21:52.019
I know because I saw it.

21:52.894 --> 21:54.479
Saw what?

21:56.815 --> 21:58.025
[sighs]

21:59.192 --> 22:00.819
All the people who want guns.

22:01.695 --> 22:03.405
And who are these people?

22:06.325 --> 22:07.409
[music fades]

22:07.492 --> 22:09.411
Isn't that your job to find out?

22:10.287 --> 22:13.373
[Yoon] That bastard is acting stupid
and playing us for a bunch of fools.

22:14.875 --> 22:18.587
Given his psychiatric history,
he's just looking to plead insanity.

22:19.379 --> 22:20.964
We should still look into it.

22:21.715 --> 22:24.301
- It could get even worse if we do nothing.
- [Yoon] Look into what?

22:24.384 --> 22:26.470
How does that even make sense?

22:26.553 --> 22:28.221
A gun? In the mail?

22:29.348 --> 22:30.349
[Seo] Hold on.

22:30.432 --> 22:32.726
You don't actually believe
what he said, do you?

22:32.809 --> 22:36.438
If he had those guns couriered to him,
how did he pay for them?

22:37.022 --> 22:39.691
He only has 530,000 won in his account.

22:39.775 --> 22:41.651
Nothing suspicious,
not even a credit card.

22:41.735 --> 22:47.407
So… who would send guns,
to a guy like that just for free?

22:48.200 --> 22:49.785
That's where we should start.

22:50.285 --> 22:52.162
Who's doing this and the reason why.

22:52.662 --> 22:54.873
[reporters clamoring]

22:54.956 --> 22:56.541
[female reporter] What was your motive?

22:59.836 --> 23:01.922
[male reporter 1]
How many people are dead?

23:03.548 --> 23:05.967
How many people are dead?
How many in the hospital?

23:06.551 --> 23:08.011
[male reporter 2] Any comment?

23:09.554 --> 23:12.015
- [clamoring continues]
- Excuse me. Captain Joo.

23:12.099 --> 23:13.141
I just have one question.

23:13.225 --> 23:15.519
- Don't bother me, kid. I'm busy.
- You heard the man.

23:17.854 --> 23:20.190
These are guns. There are more, right?

23:21.858 --> 23:24.528
This is an ongoing investigation,
so I can't comment at the moment.

23:25.320 --> 23:27.030
Why are you being so tight-lipped?

23:27.114 --> 23:29.658
I know what I saw. There are more guns.

23:29.741 --> 23:33.495
- Smuggled? Or handmade? You tell me.
- Hey, let it go!

23:34.871 --> 23:36.581
I'll write something based on this photo.

23:36.665 --> 23:40.836
You're a reporter, for God's sake.
Write articles based on fact, not fiction.

23:40.919 --> 23:43.296
- You should know better than that.
- [engine starts]

23:44.131 --> 23:47.050
If you don't tell us the facts,
I'm forced to make it up!

23:47.134 --> 23:49.136
[siren wailing]

23:50.387 --> 23:51.555
Captain!

23:56.143 --> 23:57.686
[woman sighs]

23:58.895 --> 24:00.105
Oh my!

24:00.981 --> 24:03.024
Today's rice is perfect. Hmm?

24:04.568 --> 24:05.652
I was worried,

24:06.778 --> 24:10.407
because the forecast said
it was going to rain yesterday,

24:11.450 --> 24:13.827
but it was actually very sunny.

24:15.120 --> 24:16.830
I didn't feel the cold at all.

24:16.913 --> 24:18.915
[somber music playing]

24:20.375 --> 24:23.462
Eat up, son.
And I'm gonna do my best for you today.

24:24.629 --> 24:26.882
Bye, love. You have a good day, okay?

24:28.758 --> 24:31.011
Hmm. [inhales deeply]

24:36.266 --> 24:38.185
LISTEN TO MY DEAD SON'S MESSAGE!

24:42.939 --> 24:45.108
[landlady] Well, word spread
that someone died here,

24:45.192 --> 24:46.943
so no one wants to rent it now.

24:47.027 --> 24:49.154
I'm so angry this had to happen.

24:49.654 --> 24:52.199
- I see.
- What are you looking for in there anyway?

24:52.282 --> 24:55.702
- [groans in disgust]
- Uh, we just wanted to check something.

24:55.785 --> 24:59.456
So you say no one came by to visit,
or no deliveries at all?

24:59.539 --> 25:01.166
Deliveries?

25:01.249 --> 25:03.877
I don't think he had
any friends or family.

25:09.508 --> 25:10.550
Thank you, ma'am.

25:15.472 --> 25:16.640
[sighs]

25:19.809 --> 25:20.936
[Jeong-u] Officer Lee?

25:24.481 --> 25:26.233
May I ask what you're looking at?

25:27.609 --> 25:29.194
The gosiwon over there.

25:31.071 --> 25:33.448
Do you think the shooter saying
there were more guns out there

25:33.532 --> 25:34.950
was telling the truth?

25:35.033 --> 25:37.452
I really hope
he was just making the whole thing up.

25:38.870 --> 25:40.288
[chuckles softly]

25:40.372 --> 25:41.790
Yeah. I hope so too.

25:43.166 --> 25:44.751
There's no way that guns

25:46.378 --> 25:47.879
should be so easy to get.

25:52.801 --> 25:54.803
- [boy panting]
- [indistinct chatter]

26:01.726 --> 26:02.727
[boy 1] Really?

26:03.353 --> 26:04.854
Are you fucking kidding me?

26:06.273 --> 26:07.315
[boy 1 sighs]

26:07.399 --> 26:10.694
Not a single one of these
is worth selling for shit.

26:11.403 --> 26:12.737
Do you hear what I'm telling you?

26:13.780 --> 26:15.282
Look. [sighs]

26:15.907 --> 26:16.992
These turn you on?

26:17.576 --> 26:21.162
How long are you gonna take
worthless photos like these, huh?

26:21.246 --> 26:22.956
It's about fucking time!

26:23.039 --> 26:25.417
Your friend here is
having trouble breathing.

26:25.500 --> 26:27.335
- You better hurry, fat-ass!
- [boy 3] Come on!

26:27.419 --> 26:29.337
Hurry your ass. He's gonna die, man.

26:29.421 --> 26:31.965
- [choking]
- You wanna have that on your conscience?

26:32.048 --> 26:33.633
Run, run, run, run!

26:33.717 --> 26:35.802
Faster! Faster, you prick! Run!

26:35.885 --> 26:36.803
What are you doing?

26:36.886 --> 26:38.013
[boy 4 groans]

26:38.096 --> 26:40.056
[breathing heavily]

26:40.140 --> 26:41.516
[panting]

26:41.600 --> 26:42.767
Take it.

26:42.851 --> 26:44.185
Here. That's everything.

26:44.269 --> 26:45.103
Hey.

26:45.186 --> 26:47.355
[somber music playing]

26:47.439 --> 26:49.691
[boy 4 panting]

26:49.774 --> 26:50.984
[boy 1] Get up, fat-ass.

26:54.237 --> 26:55.280
So, asshole…

26:57.824 --> 27:01.745
I told you to create ten accounts for me.
But you haven't done it yet.

27:02.287 --> 27:05.498
Seong-jun, I'm sorry.
I'll make them right now.

27:05.582 --> 27:07.083
It'll be really fast.

27:09.502 --> 27:10.337
[sighs]

27:10.420 --> 27:12.297
I told you to buy this,
and it's still for sale.

27:13.715 --> 27:15.759
I'll work really hard. I promise.

27:18.011 --> 27:19.929
[inhales sharply] We'll do our best.

27:25.644 --> 27:28.897
- [boy 1] Let's get out of here.
- [boy 3] God damn, you guys are losers.

27:28.980 --> 27:31.816
[boy 5] If you don't do your job,
we'll pay your mom's restaurant a visit.

27:31.900 --> 27:34.819
- [boy 6] You stink of her side dishes.
- [boy 3] Yeah, you stink.

27:34.903 --> 27:36.905
- [Seong-jun] You're in my way.
- [boy 3] Move it, pig.

27:36.988 --> 27:40.116
- [boy 6] Let's leave these lovers alone.
- [Seong-jun] Good luck, fuckface.

27:40.200 --> 27:42.202
[panting]

27:45.705 --> 27:47.123
[both groaning]

27:48.166 --> 27:49.542
I'm sorry, Gyu-Jin.

27:50.710 --> 27:52.921
I'll try to run faster next time.

27:57.175 --> 27:58.593
Take this for the blood.

28:04.516 --> 28:05.517
Thanks.

28:09.729 --> 28:11.272
I hate those assholes.

28:11.356 --> 28:12.399
Be quiet.

28:13.900 --> 28:15.402
Otherwise, they might come back.

28:18.071 --> 28:19.614
[exhales] I can't breathe.

28:22.826 --> 28:24.202
[music fades]

28:26.705 --> 28:27.914
[sighs deeply]

28:27.997 --> 28:30.166
I can't fucking breathe
with this thing on.

28:33.670 --> 28:34.754
[woman 1] That's him, right?

28:34.838 --> 28:36.715
He's so ashamed,
he has to keep his face covered.

28:36.798 --> 28:37.882
[woman 2] You're right.

28:37.966 --> 28:40.260
Why does someone like that
have to live in our neighborhood?

28:40.760 --> 28:42.053
I don't feel safe anymore.

28:42.137 --> 28:43.304
[women gasp]

28:44.848 --> 28:46.391
[woman 3 humming innocently]

28:48.309 --> 28:50.019
[Won-seong] Fucking bitches.

28:53.106 --> 28:54.232
[bottles clink]

28:54.941 --> 28:57.861
Hey, give me two packs of Marlboro Red.

29:01.740 --> 29:04.409
[clerk] You'll have to remove your mask
and show me your ID.

29:06.828 --> 29:08.371
Are you fucking kidding me?

29:10.123 --> 29:12.041
Do I look like a high schooler to you?

29:12.125 --> 29:14.502
No, uh, it's just store policy.

29:14.586 --> 29:17.172
Just give me
the fucking cigarettes already.

29:17.255 --> 29:19.299
- Uh--
- I haven't done anything wrong.

29:19.382 --> 29:21.509
- I just came here to buy stuff.
- Um…

29:21.593 --> 29:24.929
Why the fuck are you all looking at me
like I did something wrong?

29:27.807 --> 29:28.683
[sighs]

29:29.309 --> 29:31.352
I could kill everyone in that place.
[laughs]

29:33.480 --> 29:34.397
[grunts]

29:34.481 --> 29:36.149
Son of a bitch!

29:40.361 --> 29:41.863
Why all the packages?!

29:42.739 --> 29:44.616
You can't block the way
to someone's house!

29:44.699 --> 29:46.534
If you ordered shit,
you should take them in

29:46.618 --> 29:48.328
as soon as they arrive!

29:48.912 --> 29:50.872
Who the fuck are these addressed to?

29:52.040 --> 29:52.916
Park Kyeong-ja.

29:53.541 --> 29:55.502
[Ji-yeong] Is this
Park Kyeong-ja's residence?

29:55.585 --> 29:57.837
[Won-seong] My mom went to get groceries.
Come in.

29:57.921 --> 29:58.922
Oh, okay.

29:59.923 --> 30:02.050
This is for your mother.
Like me to bring it in?

30:02.133 --> 30:04.427
Nah, it's fine, you know, I…
Please come in.

30:05.929 --> 30:07.055
[uneasy music playing]

30:07.138 --> 30:09.641
Holy shit. The fuck?

30:12.143 --> 30:14.103
You can't be fucking serious.

30:20.360 --> 30:21.945
This is crazy.

30:25.114 --> 30:26.074
Oh!

30:26.699 --> 30:28.868
They sent both a K1 and K2.

30:30.161 --> 30:32.622
[chuckling]

30:33.873 --> 30:35.875
[gun parts clicking]

30:42.674 --> 30:44.676
[uneasy music continues]

30:53.935 --> 30:56.271
[music intensifies]

30:56.354 --> 30:57.438
[gun clicks]

31:01.526 --> 31:03.528
[music fades]

31:03.611 --> 31:05.196
[indistinct chatter]

31:06.990 --> 31:09.284
[laughing, hollering]

31:12.579 --> 31:14.372
Go! [groans]

31:14.455 --> 31:15.999
[man 1] Hey. Move. Move.

31:16.082 --> 31:18.543
- [man 2] Oh, this is gonna be fun.
- [man 3] Great.

31:18.626 --> 31:21.087
- [man 4] Well, hello there.
- [captive] Jeong-man!

31:21.170 --> 31:22.088
[man 1 laughing]

31:22.171 --> 31:23.840
Please! You have to listen to me!

31:24.674 --> 31:25.717
Jeong-man!

31:25.800 --> 31:27.010
You can't do this.

31:27.093 --> 31:27.927
[men laughing]

31:28.011 --> 31:28.845
Please!

31:28.928 --> 31:31.723
[sighs] First of all,
stop calling out my name.

31:32.348 --> 31:35.560
Save your last breaths.
I've got a job to do.

31:36.269 --> 31:39.147
I know. You're really good at your job.

31:40.440 --> 31:42.609
Everyone knows how smart you are. Hmm?

31:42.692 --> 31:44.569
[whimpers] With your brains,

31:45.486 --> 31:47.947
you could do so much better
than being Seok-ho's muscle.

31:49.282 --> 31:52.076
Seok-ho said he'd hand over his business.

31:52.702 --> 31:55.204
All you have to do
is get rid of me, right?

31:55.288 --> 31:57.916
But he's handing his business
over to Yong-gu.

31:58.541 --> 31:59.959
It's what I heard him say.

32:00.460 --> 32:02.545
He's never gonna let you be the boss!

32:02.629 --> 32:03.630
Mr. Kim,

32:04.255 --> 32:06.132
are you trying to hurt my feelings?

32:06.633 --> 32:09.427
- [man 5] Hurry up and bury him! Come on!
- [man 3] Let's do this!

32:09.510 --> 32:12.055
[man 5] We need to get out of here
before sunrise. Get a move on!

32:12.138 --> 32:13.806
[captive] We've known each other
ten years!

32:13.890 --> 32:16.267
Don't worry, we promise to hold
a nice funeral in your honor.

32:16.351 --> 32:20.021
Let me live, and I'll give you
a useful piece of information!

32:20.104 --> 32:22.315
[man 6] Bastards in your shoes
would say anything to live.

32:22.398 --> 32:23.232
Listen!

32:24.359 --> 32:25.693
It's not too late!

32:26.194 --> 32:29.113
- You can take over everything! Jeong-man!
- [unsettling music playing]

32:29.197 --> 32:32.033
- I swear, I can get you a gun!
- [man 3] Shut him up!

32:32.116 --> 32:35.787
You want one, it's yours.
A gun in your hand by tomorrow!

32:35.870 --> 32:38.247
- [man 3] Oh boy… [laughs]
- [captive] Jeong-man!

32:38.957 --> 32:39.916
Please!

32:39.999 --> 32:41.584
[eerie music playing]

32:41.668 --> 32:45.254
Don't listen to him.
Let's just bury him and be done with it.

32:45.838 --> 32:48.758
If the boss finds out
Mr. Kim is still alive, we're all fucked.

32:49.258 --> 32:50.677
You have to believe me. Huh?

32:50.760 --> 32:52.762
You can take over the whole thing.

32:52.845 --> 32:55.431
[man 5] Come on. A gun?
You have to be out of your mind.

32:56.265 --> 32:58.643
- [sighs]
- Let's get this over with, huh?

32:58.726 --> 33:02.063
- Listen to me. I wouldn't lie about this.
- [man 5] Fine, let's say we get a gun.

33:02.146 --> 33:03.398
What are we supposed to do,

33:03.481 --> 33:05.108
just walk right in there
with a single gun?

33:05.191 --> 33:08.653
- You know how many people work there?
- [Kim] Not just one gun! A hundred!

33:08.736 --> 33:10.154
More than a hundred. Way more.

33:10.238 --> 33:11.864
- A massive amount.
- [man 5] Shut up!

33:11.948 --> 33:14.033
- Do you think we're a bunch of idiots?
- [phone buzzing]

33:14.117 --> 33:16.494
- Give me a second.
- [man 5 sighs] Come on, man.

33:17.286 --> 33:19.580
- [Kim] What's your name?
- [man 7] None of your business.

33:19.664 --> 33:21.457
- Sir.
- [Seok-ho] Why haven't you reported back?

33:21.541 --> 33:22.375
Don't hurt me!

33:22.458 --> 33:25.336
Oh, I was just about to call you.
We're just finishing up.

33:26.295 --> 33:27.422
- Sir…
- Yeah?

33:28.756 --> 33:31.300
About the business you promised me
once this job was done…

33:31.384 --> 33:32.301
Promise?

33:33.136 --> 33:35.054
Oh, that. Listen, I'm busy right now.

33:35.138 --> 33:36.597
- We'll talk.
- [line disconnects]

33:39.976 --> 33:41.769
[Kim] He didn't answer you, did he?

33:43.021 --> 33:44.981
I told you I'm not a liar.

33:47.775 --> 33:48.818
[laughs]

33:49.444 --> 33:50.820
Son of a bitch.

33:52.447 --> 33:53.406
[metallic scraping]

33:53.489 --> 33:55.658
Jeong-man! Jeong-man! Jeong-man, no!

33:56.576 --> 33:59.162
[man 2 laughing] Oh-ho-ho-ho! Yeah!

33:59.245 --> 34:01.164
Well, what are you waiting for?
Let's bury him.

34:01.247 --> 34:02.248
[man 2] Yeah!

34:03.499 --> 34:05.585
[man 5] Hurry this up. I'm freezing here.

34:06.127 --> 34:07.211
Put him in.

34:08.671 --> 34:10.423
[man 8] I wanna eat something first.

34:10.923 --> 34:12.925
[music fades]

34:13.009 --> 34:15.011
[breathing heavily]

34:18.723 --> 34:21.809
[phone buzzing]

34:21.893 --> 34:24.395
Ah shit! Why can't you leave me alone?

34:27.940 --> 34:29.108
What do you want?

34:29.192 --> 34:31.944
[man] This is your probation officer.
Where are you now?

34:32.445 --> 34:35.114
Oh, fuck off.
You monitor me 24 hours a day.

34:35.198 --> 34:36.866
it's not like you don't know where I am.

34:36.949 --> 34:40.620
Exactly. Why are you
somewhere you don't usually frequent?

34:40.703 --> 34:42.288
Why are you up that mountain?

34:42.789 --> 34:45.249
I came here to get some fresh air.
Is that a crime?

34:45.333 --> 34:47.418
You people are always suffocating me.

34:48.753 --> 34:49.587
Hey.

34:50.463 --> 34:51.881
Let me ask you a question.

34:52.799 --> 34:57.178
Where the hell are you guys
monitoring me from anyway? Huh?

34:57.720 --> 35:00.014
Tell me, where are you hiding?

35:00.098 --> 35:02.433
I can't share that information.

35:02.517 --> 35:04.435
Oh, you can't share that information?

35:04.519 --> 35:06.312
I'm done talking to you, jackass!

35:07.271 --> 35:08.272
[scoffs]

35:17.698 --> 35:19.617
WARNING
THIS IS A MILITARY OPERATION ZONE

35:19.700 --> 35:21.536
UNAUTHORIZED ENTRY
AND PHOTOGRAPHY PROHIBITED

35:21.619 --> 35:24.038
[man] Marksmen! On my order,
get ready to fire!

35:24.122 --> 35:26.124
[distant gunfire]

35:32.004 --> 35:34.340
[distant gunfire continues]

35:34.423 --> 35:36.008
[unsettling music playing]

35:41.013 --> 35:43.015
[distant gunfire continues]

35:43.099 --> 35:45.101
[laughing]

35:46.352 --> 35:48.563
I haven't lost my touch at all.

35:48.646 --> 35:50.231
[man] Prepare to fire!

35:50.982 --> 35:53.818
Marksmen! When you're ready, fire!

35:53.901 --> 35:55.361
[distant automatic gunfire]

36:01.826 --> 36:03.494
[laughing manically]

36:03.578 --> 36:05.246
- [laughter echoing]
- [music fades]

36:05.329 --> 36:07.331
[keyboard clacking]

36:11.127 --> 36:12.712
- I admire you, Officer Lee.
- [gasps]

36:13.212 --> 36:14.297
[sighs deeply]

36:15.756 --> 36:16.799
[sighs]

36:18.634 --> 36:20.720
Uh, the list of reported firearms
I asked you for…

36:20.803 --> 36:21.637
Here you go.

36:23.931 --> 36:25.224
- [officer] Lee.
- Yes?

36:26.184 --> 36:28.895
Did you request a list of items
cleared by customs? Here.

36:28.978 --> 36:32.148
Yes, there's something that's bugging me.
I just wanted to check it out.

36:32.231 --> 36:34.150
I mean,
it's good to see you working so hard,

36:34.233 --> 36:36.527
but maybe let
the detectives do the sleuthing?

36:36.611 --> 36:38.196
We shouldn't be stepping on any toes.

36:39.322 --> 36:41.032
I won't be. No need to worry.

36:41.115 --> 36:42.658
All right, I'll leave you to it.

36:42.742 --> 36:44.535
- [Do] Thanks again.
- [officer] Sure.

36:51.334 --> 36:56.214
CUSTOMS CLEARANCE LIST
FIREARMS

36:56.297 --> 36:59.175
How come you haven't been
answering your phone? Huh?

36:59.258 --> 37:00.426
And why are you so late?

37:00.927 --> 37:03.846
Well, it took longer than expected
to wrap everything up.

37:03.930 --> 37:05.890
You should've called earlier
to let me know.

37:05.973 --> 37:08.059
- I hate waiting.
- Here's the picture of Mr. Kim.

37:09.518 --> 37:12.730
Whoa, shit!
That's one hell of a photo you took.

37:12.813 --> 37:13.773
[Seok-ho chuckling]

37:13.856 --> 37:14.774
Wow.

37:14.857 --> 37:16.359
You've got some talent.

37:16.442 --> 37:18.194
Maybe you missed your calling, huh?

37:18.277 --> 37:19.278
[chuckling]

37:19.362 --> 37:20.446
Here.

37:20.529 --> 37:23.199
- [man 1] The food here is good.
- [man 2] That means you're buying?

37:23.282 --> 37:24.825
- Get out of here, you.
- Jeez.

37:27.662 --> 37:28.704
[exhales nervously]

37:35.253 --> 37:36.420
- Jeong-man.
- Yeah?

37:36.504 --> 37:38.005
It's nice here, isn't it?

37:38.089 --> 37:39.215
- Yes, sir.
- [chuckling]

37:39.966 --> 37:41.300
So does that mean

37:42.510 --> 37:45.888
that me and my boys
get to run this place from now on,

37:45.972 --> 37:47.181
seeing as the job is over?

37:47.265 --> 37:49.141
What the hell are you on about? [scoffs]

37:49.642 --> 37:51.477
Yong-gu's going to manage this place.

37:51.560 --> 37:52.395
[Seok-ho chuckles]

37:52.478 --> 37:54.897
- What?
- You're not ready for that yet.

37:54.981 --> 37:57.316
[man 1] Come on, man, trust me.
This is legit information.

37:57.400 --> 37:58.776
[man 2] Sounds too good to be true.

37:58.859 --> 38:00.861
[suspenseful music playing]

38:04.282 --> 38:05.741
Ah, fuck me!

38:05.825 --> 38:07.743
[breathing nervously]

38:09.328 --> 38:10.246
What?

38:11.497 --> 38:14.542
Well, you promised me last time we spoke

38:14.625 --> 38:16.711
that you'd let us run
one of your businesses for you.

38:16.794 --> 38:18.796
[laughing]

38:18.879 --> 38:20.172
Listen to me.

38:20.256 --> 38:23.217
This here is money.
Your kind don't fit here, you see?

38:25.594 --> 38:26.595
[sighs]

38:27.096 --> 38:28.139
The thing is,

38:29.265 --> 38:31.934
my boys and I,
you don't know how hard we worked.

38:32.018 --> 38:33.769
We killed for you.

38:34.270 --> 38:36.105
Anything you asked, we would do.

38:36.605 --> 38:38.899
- You can always rely on us--
- Cut the shit.

38:40.067 --> 38:41.777
Okay? You're mine.

38:44.989 --> 38:47.116
Just give us a chance to live like humans.

38:47.199 --> 38:48.784
"Humans"? [scoffs]

38:50.036 --> 38:51.912
What have you been all this time, then?

38:51.996 --> 38:53.039
[chuckles softly]

38:54.540 --> 38:57.043
Haven't we always just been
your obedient mutts?

38:57.543 --> 38:59.712
[tense music playing]

38:59.795 --> 39:00.796
"Mutts"?

39:02.131 --> 39:03.466
Is that what you think you are?

39:13.142 --> 39:15.144
Ah! Fucking shit!

39:15.227 --> 39:18.647
Why do you have to be so serious?
You're making me feel so bad now.

39:19.440 --> 39:20.274
Fine, all right?

39:20.358 --> 39:22.651
Let's see how I can make this up
to you guys another day.

39:22.735 --> 39:24.195
Just don't be an asshole.

39:25.196 --> 39:26.030
Okay?

39:29.492 --> 39:31.035
I… I have one last question.

39:31.869 --> 39:34.705
Do you happen to know
the name of any of my boys?

39:34.789 --> 39:37.500
Why? Is there someone in the group
you think I should know?

39:38.250 --> 39:40.795
It's only because
they're all working so hard for you.

39:40.878 --> 39:43.756
It would mean a lot
if you at least refer to them by name.

39:43.839 --> 39:45.091
[Seok-ho] All right. Here.

39:45.174 --> 39:47.176
Take this, and go get some food.

39:47.259 --> 39:50.262
All of you eat,
and maybe take a goddamn bath.

39:50.346 --> 39:52.098
You stink like shit.

39:52.181 --> 39:53.474
Very kind, sir.

39:55.976 --> 39:58.521
Hey! Hey. Toss that on your way out.

39:58.604 --> 39:59.563
PRESIDENT KIM DEOK-HYEON

39:59.647 --> 40:00.940
Don't want his ghost haunting me.

40:01.023 --> 40:02.942
- [man 1] Does this hurt?
- Ow! Of course it hurts!

40:03.025 --> 40:07.530
- Hey, cut it out! I told you it hurts.
- [man 1] Baby. I hardly touched you.

40:08.406 --> 40:09.865
[man 3] He's here! He's here!

40:09.949 --> 40:11.117
[man 4] Bravo!

40:11.200 --> 40:13.869
Jeong-man, are we ready
to move into this place or what?

40:13.953 --> 40:15.287
- [man 5] Let's party!
- [laughter]

40:15.371 --> 40:16.914
Hold on. What's this?

40:16.997 --> 40:17.915
You don't look happy.

40:19.500 --> 40:20.334
[Jeong-man] Yong-gu

40:21.836 --> 40:24.130
and his boys are in charge from now on.

40:24.213 --> 40:26.257
I should've known
you'd backstab us, Seok-ho!

40:26.340 --> 40:28.092
- For real? How?
- U-tae.

40:29.677 --> 40:32.179
- You search inside?
- There's a storage room.

40:32.847 --> 40:33.973
I couldn't get in.

40:34.723 --> 40:37.059
Hey, Kim almost shit his pants
going into that hole.

40:37.143 --> 40:39.186
What if he just fed us
a bunch of bullshit?

40:39.270 --> 40:40.729
I don't wanna start all over again.

40:41.230 --> 40:42.440
- Chang-ju.
- Yeah?

40:42.523 --> 40:44.733
Take the others
to that gosiwon on the news.

40:44.817 --> 40:47.653
See if there's anything salvageable.
You, come with me.

40:47.736 --> 40:49.280
- [man 3 groans]
- Hey! Hey, hey.

40:49.363 --> 40:50.948
- You heard the man.
- [Jeong-man] Guys.

40:51.031 --> 40:53.367
[suspenseful music playing]

40:53.451 --> 40:55.202
Take this and get cleaned up,

40:55.703 --> 40:57.079
and get some good food.

40:58.164 --> 40:59.957
I'm sorry things turned out
the way they did.

41:00.040 --> 41:01.167
[Chang-ju] It's all right.

41:01.959 --> 41:03.711
- Don't worry.
- [Jeong-man] See you guys later.

41:03.794 --> 41:05.504
- Hey, wait up.
- [man 4] Let's go.

41:08.632 --> 41:11.177
Hey, what's gotten into you?
What is it, hmm?

41:11.260 --> 41:13.846
Come on, enough with the secrets. Jeong!

41:15.055 --> 41:17.850
- You know where Mr. Kim's car is?
- Yeah. Why?

41:19.018 --> 41:20.019
Let's check it.

41:22.146 --> 41:23.606
[engine starts]

41:31.655 --> 41:33.657
[music fades]

41:35.701 --> 41:37.703
[distant sirens wailing]

41:56.764 --> 41:57.890
[phone buzzes]

42:01.477 --> 42:04.939
[Seong-jun] Fuck-gyu.
Get your mom's ID and get over here now.

42:08.192 --> 42:10.110
- [woman 1] Enjoy.
- [man 1] The rolled omelet?

42:10.194 --> 42:12.530
Of course. One rolled omelet, please!

42:12.613 --> 42:13.697
[man 2] Dessert is on me.

42:13.781 --> 42:15.032
DAESEONG RESTAURANT

42:15.115 --> 42:16.617
- [woman 2] Thank you.
- [man 2] I'm glad…

42:21.705 --> 42:23.207
- [woman 2] That's too bad
- [woman 1] Oh!

42:23.290 --> 42:24.208
Hi.

42:24.917 --> 42:26.126
[woman 1 chuckles softly]

42:26.752 --> 42:29.129
What's wrong?
You look so nervous, sweetie.

42:29.213 --> 42:31.131
Whatever it is, you can tell me.

42:32.174 --> 42:34.051
Could I borrow some money?

42:34.635 --> 42:35.678
How much money?

42:36.345 --> 42:37.346
[inhales sharply]

42:38.138 --> 42:41.475
Why do you suddenly need money?
Is something going on?

42:42.935 --> 42:44.728
No, um, I just need money.

42:45.312 --> 42:46.355
Really, I'm fine.

42:48.482 --> 42:49.858
Are you sure you're okay?

42:50.985 --> 42:52.653
Yes, I'm more than okay.

42:54.238 --> 42:55.114
Forget it.

42:55.614 --> 42:57.116
[woman 1] You're a good boy. It's fine.

42:57.199 --> 42:59.285
I'm busy,
so grab whatever you need from my wallet.

42:59.368 --> 43:02.079
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD
HONG, SEO-JEONG

43:03.080 --> 43:06.417
- [woman 2] Thanks for the food, ma'am!
- [Seo-jeong] See you soon!

43:17.803 --> 43:20.139
- I'm gonna get going.
- Oh! Okay.

43:23.601 --> 43:25.644
[door opens, closes]

43:25.728 --> 43:28.689
- [muffled upbeat music playing]
- [boys chattering, laughing]

43:35.404 --> 43:37.448
[boy 1] Hey, here comes Gyu!

43:37.531 --> 43:40.284
- [indistinct chatter]
- [upbeat music continues]

43:40.784 --> 43:42.328
- [boy 2] You got it.
- [boy 3] Got it.

43:43.746 --> 43:44.747
[boy 2] Yeah!

43:50.836 --> 43:52.379
[Seong-jun] Did you bring what I asked?

43:52.463 --> 43:54.965
- [upbeat music continues]
- [boys singing karaoke]

44:00.596 --> 44:01.430
[boy 4] Hey!

44:05.392 --> 44:06.435
[music stops]

44:10.814 --> 44:12.274
So Fuck-gyu wants to die.

44:13.817 --> 44:14.652
You wanna die?

44:14.735 --> 44:16.570
Uh, well, actually…

44:17.237 --> 44:18.614
[microphone feedback rings]

44:21.158 --> 44:22.743
[unsettling music playing]

44:25.621 --> 44:27.998
- [grunting]
- [Seong-jun] Am I a joke to you?

44:28.082 --> 44:30.626
I mean, I couldn't get my mom's ID, so…

44:30.709 --> 44:32.336
Then steal the whole fucking wallet!

44:34.296 --> 44:36.298
[breathing anxiously]

44:40.552 --> 44:42.680
I… I… I really…

44:42.763 --> 44:43.806
I'm very sorry…

44:46.600 --> 44:49.436
But you're gonna use the ID to borrow
money from a loan shark. Right?

44:52.189 --> 44:54.608
My mom, she works so hard.

44:55.901 --> 44:58.570
What if I just tried to make
the photos racier?

44:59.446 --> 45:00.364
[grunts]

45:01.907 --> 45:04.868
Do you honestly think I give a fuck
how hard your mom works?

45:06.829 --> 45:07.663
Okay…

45:07.746 --> 45:09.498
I don't give a shit.

45:10.416 --> 45:11.333
I know.

45:12.209 --> 45:13.460
[Seong-jun] So let's try again.

45:13.961 --> 45:16.338
Can you bring her ID to me tomorrow?

45:19.174 --> 45:20.092
[splutters]

45:22.469 --> 45:23.721
Is that a yes or a no?

45:25.264 --> 45:26.265
I, uh…

45:26.348 --> 45:29.435
- [groans]
- Yes or no, you fucking loser?

45:29.935 --> 45:31.812
Um… I don't know.

45:32.312 --> 45:33.647
Don't make me angry!

45:34.982 --> 45:36.525
Time to fuck you up.

45:37.109 --> 45:39.236
[Gyu-jin grunting, groaning]

45:39.319 --> 45:42.030
[boy 2] Loser! Nothing but a mama's boy.

45:45.200 --> 45:47.202
- [music fades]
- [tires screech]

45:56.128 --> 45:57.796
[U-tae] We gotta find the keys!

45:57.880 --> 45:59.798
- The keys!
- [Jeong-man] Check the tires!

45:59.882 --> 46:01.133
Look for them!

46:03.093 --> 46:05.012
[sighs angrily] Where the fuck are they?

46:06.555 --> 46:08.348
Found them!
I got 'em, I got 'em, I got 'em!

46:08.849 --> 46:09.683
Open it.

46:12.227 --> 46:13.312
Move!

46:18.567 --> 46:20.736
[U-tae breathing nervously]

46:22.863 --> 46:23.989
[tense music playing]

46:24.072 --> 46:25.908
[U-tae] Oh… Holy shit!

46:33.582 --> 46:34.666
No!

46:38.962 --> 46:39.880
Jeong-man!

46:40.964 --> 46:42.633
We… we should think about this.

46:42.716 --> 46:43.842
You can't be rash!

46:45.803 --> 46:49.848
No! How stupid does this make us, huh?
What are we going to do with one gun?

46:50.724 --> 46:53.769
If things go wrong,
the two of us are seriously fucked!

46:53.852 --> 46:56.563
Okay, then what?
You wanna keep waiting for scraps?

46:56.647 --> 46:58.440
- [exhales sharply]
- U-tae.

46:59.733 --> 47:01.693
That prick will never let us grow.

47:02.194 --> 47:06.490
Do what you're told, have more patience…
It's just… That should be my business!

47:06.990 --> 47:08.116
[exhales forcefully]

47:08.200 --> 47:09.868
You, us,

47:10.619 --> 47:11.703
all our boys.

47:12.412 --> 47:15.624
That bastard's dangling a treat
with no intention of giving it.

47:16.708 --> 47:18.335
Wanna be a gofer forever?

47:19.211 --> 47:21.213
- F… fuck.
- Living like this?

47:22.965 --> 47:24.258
[lock clicks]

47:31.306 --> 47:32.140
U-tae.

47:34.935 --> 47:35.894
I see this…

47:39.523 --> 47:40.899
as an opportunity.

47:41.525 --> 47:43.527
[breathing deeply]

47:45.821 --> 47:47.823
[tense music continues]

47:55.789 --> 47:56.874
[music fades]

48:00.627 --> 48:02.212
[Do] Where did you get the gun?

48:02.838 --> 48:04.006
It was couriered to me.

48:04.506 --> 48:08.176
Why would a stranger send you
a package with a gun in it by courier?

48:08.260 --> 48:09.386
The truth.

48:10.053 --> 48:12.055
[intriguing music playing]

48:14.266 --> 48:16.101
Ever received a package
from an unknown sender?

48:16.184 --> 48:17.019
I don't know.

48:22.983 --> 48:24.860
[Do] Around what time
does the courier come?

48:24.943 --> 48:26.278
[man 1] Between 2:00 and 4:00 p.m.

48:26.361 --> 48:27.195
YEONGSEONG GOSIWON

48:27.279 --> 48:29.531
- [Do] Seen this man around here?
- [man 2] Uh, no.

48:29.615 --> 48:32.034
[Do] Which day of the week
does the recycling get picked up?

48:32.117 --> 48:33.827
[woman] Tuesdays and Thursdays.

48:41.877 --> 48:44.171
- [man 1] Sure you looked up there?
- [man 2] There's nothing.

48:44.254 --> 48:45.505
[man 3] I already checked.

48:45.589 --> 48:48.258
[man 4] Where the hell is it?
Seriously, are we sure he wasn't lying?

48:48.842 --> 48:51.637
[man 1] No, he said it was here.
Wait, hold on.

48:51.720 --> 48:52.763
This…

48:52.846 --> 48:54.181
No, this isn't it. Jesus!

48:54.264 --> 48:56.391
- [man 4] Hey--
- [Do] This is the police.

48:57.142 --> 48:58.393
What are you doing here?

48:59.394 --> 49:00.520
[man 1] Uh,

49:01.271 --> 49:04.024
we were gonna make some cash
selling boxes.

49:04.107 --> 49:05.901
- Got a problem with that?
- [man 5] Here we go.

49:05.984 --> 49:08.612
- [men chuckling]
- [Do] Didn't you see the tape back there?

49:09.613 --> 49:11.990
This is a crime scene.
You can't just come in here.

49:12.074 --> 49:14.076
- [man 1] I don't know how to read.
- [man 2] Dumbass.

49:14.159 --> 49:15.369
Our mistake, Officer.

49:36.765 --> 49:38.767
[phone buzzing]

49:43.647 --> 49:44.481
Yes, Captain?

49:44.564 --> 49:46.984
So you know
all that stuff the kid told us?

49:47.067 --> 49:49.319
I don't think we have to worry about it.
It was all lies.

49:49.903 --> 49:50.737
What?

49:50.821 --> 49:52.739
We ran the records
of all the courier companies,

49:52.823 --> 49:55.742
and there's no record of anything
being sent to his address.

49:56.243 --> 49:59.705
In fact, he hasn't received
a single package in the last three years.

49:59.788 --> 50:01.498
He keeps saying all this weird stuff

50:01.581 --> 50:05.419
about how everyone's got a trigger
in their hearts, or some crazy shit.

50:06.044 --> 50:07.462
None of it is useful.

50:07.963 --> 50:10.257
Anyway, we'll recheck the security cams

50:10.340 --> 50:13.635
and the nearby vehicles
and I'll let you know if we find anything.

50:13.719 --> 50:15.387
[sighs] Thank you, sir.

50:16.596 --> 50:17.597
Anything else,

50:19.016 --> 50:20.851
you can just give me a call.

50:21.935 --> 50:23.729
I appreciate all your support.

50:23.812 --> 50:25.564
Okay, thanks. Have a good one.

50:39.953 --> 50:41.288
[tense music playing]

50:51.965 --> 50:53.967
[tense music continues]

50:57.763 --> 50:59.765
[car horn honking]

51:02.392 --> 51:03.310
NAME: JEON WON-SEONG

51:03.393 --> 51:05.437
[Seo] 23S-249.
That's Won-seong's car, right?

51:05.520 --> 51:07.856
- [officer 1] Get in closer.
- What's going on?

51:08.356 --> 51:09.858
[Do] Jeong-tae did receive a package.

51:09.941 --> 51:11.193
I saw the box.

51:11.276 --> 51:14.529
And I think a man named Won-seong
got the same package.

51:14.613 --> 51:17.866
Won-seong?
He's the guy we're chasing right now.

51:18.366 --> 51:20.952
Hold on. We've almost caught up to him.
Call you when we're there.

51:21.036 --> 51:22.829
Okay. Whoa, whoa!

51:25.457 --> 51:27.084
[sirens wailing]

51:28.210 --> 51:29.419
- Go.
- [officer 2] Yes, sir!

51:29.503 --> 51:32.172
- [officer 3] Won-seong, out of the car!
- [officer 4] Hands up!

51:40.013 --> 51:43.016
[officer 3] Raise your hands!
Get out of the car! Now!

51:43.975 --> 51:45.519
- Whoa!
- Move out of the way!

51:45.602 --> 51:49.106
What's wrong? Why are you stopping me?
I haven't done anything wrong.

51:49.189 --> 51:50.023
Wait.

51:50.524 --> 51:52.400
Sir, do you know this person?

51:52.484 --> 51:54.277
We're looking for this suspect.

51:54.361 --> 51:56.404
He… got off a while back.

51:59.449 --> 52:00.450
Detective!

52:01.326 --> 52:03.745
We found Won-seong's ankle bracelet
and cell phone.

52:03.829 --> 52:05.831
[tense music continues]

52:34.109 --> 52:35.819
[music fades]

52:52.502 --> 52:54.337
[unsettling music playing]

53:11.104 --> 53:13.106
[unsettling music continues]

53:24.701 --> 53:26.703
[unsettling music continues]

53:32.209 --> 53:34.211
- [creaking]
- [music fades]

53:47.015 --> 53:48.141
[creaking]

53:50.227 --> 53:52.562
[dramatic music playing]

54:05.700 --> 54:06.534
[music fades]

54:06.618 --> 54:08.536
- Who are you?
- [grunts] That hurts!

54:10.288 --> 54:11.122
Wait!

54:11.206 --> 54:13.333
- [sweeping music playing]
- My name's Moon Baek.

54:13.833 --> 54:14.793
Moon Baek!

54:15.502 --> 54:16.711
What are you doing here?

54:16.795 --> 54:18.088
[groans] I-- I…

54:19.714 --> 54:21.716
I came to pick something up.

54:21.800 --> 54:23.051
A… a package.

54:25.512 --> 54:27.514
[funky rock music playing]

56:55.078 --> 56:55.954
[music fades]

56:56.037 --> 56:58.039
[dramatic music playing]

58:24.542 --> 58:26.544
[music fades]
